As Dairon suggested, using a single api might be anti pattern coz consolidating all other api calls at bff layer would need the response in bff to indicate success objects of successful api and error calls of errored apis. For example, 
```
{
success: {api-call-1: {}, api-calls-2: {}},
error: {api-call-3: {}, api-calls-4: {}}
}
```
Then bff would say 200 response and code would still be checking for error in the response body. On the other hand, we can also strongly discuss saying why we can do this. But I felt it would be a lot more easier to handle error scenarios if we have separate calls and it will be only 3 api calls. So followed the separate api approach.
